912
00:37:57,618 --> 00:37:59,238
I think that the quality of my life depends on,

913
00:37:59,238 --> 00:38:00,198
I think,

914
00:38:00,198 --> 00:38:02,038
the quality of my life depends on the quality

915
00:38:02,038 --> 00:38:03,698
of everyone else's.

916
00:38:03,698 --> 00:38:07,018
So if we provide preventative care now,

917
00:38:07,018 --> 00:38:10,257
then the cost of expensive treatments down the line

918
00:38:10,257 --> 00:38:11,418
will be lower.

919
00:38:11,418 --> 00:38:13,877
And if we provide care to everyone,

920
00:38:13,877 --> 00:38:17,577
I won't be exposed to contagious diseases as much.

921
00:38:17,577 --> 00:38:21,837
So I think that universal healthcare is a matter

922
00:38:21,837 --> 00:38:26,837
of increasing the common good of the entire society.

923
00:38:27,138 --> 00:38:28,318
And you say, Skyler,

924
00:38:28,318 --> 00:38:30,138
it's a matter of increasing the common good,

925
00:38:30,138 --> 00:38:32,998
because it will promote public health,

926
00:38:32,998 --> 00:38:35,678
it'll prevent epidemics, that sort of thing?

927
00:38:35,678 --> 00:38:36,518
Exactly.

928
00:38:36,518 --> 00:38:39,578
And what do you think about Alex's suggestion

929
00:38:39,578 --> 00:38:43,098
that the common good requires that members

930
00:38:43,098 --> 00:38:47,558
