935
00:38:56,198 --> 00:38:59,078
It's not about feeling some sort of kinship

936
00:38:59,078 --> 00:39:00,078
with the people around you.

937
00:39:00,078 --> 00:39:03,618
Very simply, by providing this care,

938
00:39:03,618 --> 00:39:06,678
it will increase your own utility

939
00:39:06,678 --> 00:39:10,598
and help you to live a healthier existence.

940
00:39:10,598 --> 00:39:11,938
Are you happy with that, Alex?

941
00:39:11,938 --> 00:39:14,458
Well, I think sometimes when you justify it,

942
00:39:14,458 --> 00:39:15,838
even on that selfish level,

943
00:39:15,838 --> 00:39:19,758
you get bogged down in the numbers and the details.

944
00:39:19,758 --> 00:39:21,498
And I think the most solid argument

945
00:39:21,498 --> 00:39:23,618
that you could make for it is just truly

946
00:39:23,618 --> 00:39:27,398
in that ideological context of the common good.

947
00:39:27,398 --> 00:39:29,998
I think when you start estimating how much, you know,

948
00:39:29,998 --> 00:39:30,008
how much you can do for

949
00:39:30,008 --> 00:39:30,018
the community, you can do a lot.

950
00:39:30,018 --> 00:39:31,458
You can make money for the community,

951
00:39:31,458 --> 00:39:32,658
but you can also make money for yourself.

952
00:39:32,658 --> 00:39:33,938
You can produce wealth that makes you happy.

953
00:39:33,938 --> 00:39:34,698
I think if you just

954
00:39:34,698 --> 00:39:35,458
don't make enough to pay off

955
00:39:35,458 --> 00:39:36,658
how much your own livelihood will be benefited

956
00:39:36,658 --> 00:39:38,238
by your specific, you know, dollar donations

957
00:39:38,238 --> 00:39:41,658
to the common good, I think you'll be very hard-pressed

958
00:39:41,658 --> 00:39:44,038
to come up with, you know,

959
00:39:44,038 --> 00:39:46,418
a solid piece of palpable gain,

960
00:39:46,418 --> 00:39:47,758
at least in this lifetime.

961
00:39:47,758 --> 00:39:49,198
But I think it just comes down to

962
00:39:49,198 --> 00:39:51,958
that ideological difference of that.

963
00:39:51,958 --> 00:39:52,318
All right.

964
00:39:52,318 --> 00:39:59,938
So, we've actually heard three different arguments in favor

965
00:39:59,938 --> 00:40:04,938
of taxpayer-supported healthcare of one kind or another.

966
00:40:05,538 --> 00:40:07,307
I should mention that Obamacare

967
00:40:07,307 --> 00:40:09,077
is not a single-payer system.

968
00:40:09,077 --> 00:40:13,577
It doesn't create national health services in the UK.

969
00:40:13,577 --> 00:40:16,037
What it does is it leaves

970
00:40:16,037 --> 00:40:18,497
the private insurance companies in place.

971
00:40:18,497 --> 00:40:21,297
It requires those companies to accept

972
00:40:21,297 --> 00:40:24,097
everyone who wants to apply for healthcare,

973
00:40:24,097 --> 00:40:27,038
regardless of pre-existing conditions.

974
