And in return, it tells the health insurance companies,

975
00:40:32,938 --> 00:40:34,898
you'll get a lot more customers

976
00:40:34,898 --> 00:40:36,858
because we are also going to require

977
00:40:36,858 --> 00:40:41,538
that everyone must carry health insurance,

978
00:40:41,538 --> 00:40:45,178
must buy health insurance of one kind or another.

979
00:40:45,178 --> 00:40:48,138
But I've heard here three different arguments

980
00:40:48,138 --> 00:40:53,898
in favor of government-supported healthcare.

981
00:40:53,898 --> 00:40:56,717
One argument is a practical argument.

982
00:40:56,717 --> 00:40:56,918
It's a practical argument.

983
00:40:56,918 --> 00:40:56,998
It's a practical argument. It's a practical argument.

984
00:40:56,998 --> 00:40:57,018
It's a practical argument. It's a practical argument.

985
00:40:57,018 --> 00:41:01,718
It's a public health argument that costs will be lower

986
00:41:01,718 --> 00:41:03,998
and the public health will

987
00:41:03,998 --> 00:41:06,278
be higher if everybody is covered.

988
00:41:06,278 --> 00:41:08,998
That's an argument which doesn't

989
00:41:08,998 --> 00:41:11,718
