1026
00:42:55,698 --> 00:42:55,758
So next slide, please.

1027
00:42:55,758 --> 00:42:55,878
Okay, so this is the first argument that we have.

1028
00:42:55,878 --> 00:42:55,948
So I want to draw some attention to the

1029
00:42:55,948 --> 00:42:56,018
fact that this argument is actually a key argument.

1030
00:42:56,018 --> 00:42:56,038
The second argument is that we have an

1031
00:42:56,038 --> 00:42:56,058
obligation to pay for the care of others.

1032
00:42:56,058 --> 00:42:56,188
The third argument is that we have a

1033
00:42:56,188 --> 00:42:56,318
great responsibility to pay for the care of others.

1034
00:42:56,318 --> 00:42:56,338
It's not really a matter of

1035
00:42:56,338 --> 00:42:56,358
paying for somebody else's health care.

1036
00:42:56,398 --> 00:43:01,677
good. Now one of the arguments that

1037
00:43:01,677 --> 00:43:06,957
is still unresolved is an argument that has

1038
00:43:06,957 --> 00:43:10,087
